    {
      "text": "Figure 2: Accuracy of long-horizon dynamics prediction. We train the dynamics models on the medium",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        521.7535400390625,
        528.3047485351562,
        529.76953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dataset and evaluate on medium (training data), medium-replay (lower-quality data), and expert (higher-quality",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        532.8111572265625,
        528.7047119140625,
        540.728515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "data) datasets. Prediction errors are measured by the median root mean square deviation (RMSD) on non-",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        543.7701416015625,
        529.84765625,
        551.6875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "velocity coordinates based on 1024 sampled state action sequences of length 256. Plots show median ± 10",
      "bbox": [
        83.46099853515625,
        554.1821899414062,
        528.5318603515625,
        562.646484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "percentile bands. The multi-step diffusion dynamics model incurs significantly lower prediction error on training",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        565.6881103515625,
        528.362060546875,
        573.60546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "data while maintaining superior generalization abilities, outperforming other single-step and auto-regressive",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        576.6471557617188,
        528.3753662109375,
        584.5645141601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "alternatives. The auto-regressive transformer (ART) dynamics model outperforms the single step diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        587.6051635742188,
        528.3021850585938,
        595.5225219726562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics model. The single-step MLP dynamics model exhibits compounding errors that grow rapidly for",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        598.5641479492188,
        528.4942016601562,
        606.4815063476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "long-horizon dynamics predictions.",
      "bbox": [
        83.70099639892578,
        609.5231323242188,
        223.89962768554688,
        617.4404907226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "coordinates with increasing trajectory length. Fig. 2 summarizes the results. From the figure we can see how",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        644.1829223632812,
        540.5869140625,
        654.1455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the multi-step diffusion dynamics model reduces compounding errors in long-horizon dynamics predictions",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        656.137939453125,
        540.2323608398438,
        666.1005249023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "compared to single-step and auto-regressive alternatives, while maintaining superior generalization abilities,",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        668.0939331054688,
        541.6253662109375,
        678.0565185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "especially for action distributions that are not too far from training distributions.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        680.0488891601562,
        427.9736328125,
        690.011474609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We then evaluate the quality of these dynamics models when used inside the D-MPC planning loop with a",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        697.9808959960938,
        540.2186279296875,
        707.9434814453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "multi-step diffusion action proposal. When using the ART dynamics model, we get a score of 59.83, but when",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        709.9368896484375,
        540.1820678710938,
        719.8994750976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "using the multi-step diffusion dynamics model, we get 65.98. We believe this difference is due to the fact that",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        721.8919067382812,
        540.484619140625,
        731.8544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
